-- title:
--   Quotients of a crossing chart by U and V are polynomial rings
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $t \in W$, and write $C =$ `CrossingQuotient W t` for the quotient of the polynomial ring $W[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - t$. Let `U t` and `V t` be the two distinguished elements of $C$ attached to $t$ (the two elements whose vanishing loci are the two components of the locus $t = 0$). The theorem asserts a conjunction of two statements, symmetric in `U t` and `V t`. First, there exists an isomorphism of $W$-algebras $E$ from $C / (U t)$, the quotient of $C$ by the ideal generated by `U t`, onto the polynomial ring in one variable over $W / (t)$, the quotient of $W$ by the ideal generated by $t$, such that $E$ sends the class of `V t` modulo $(U t)$ to the polynomial indeterminate `Polynomial.X`. Second, there exists an isomorphism of $W$-algebras from $C / (V t)$ onto the same polynomial ring $(W/(t))[X]$ carrying the class of `U t` modulo $(V t)$ to `Polynomial.X`. Only existence of such isomorphisms, together with the stated value on one generator, is asserted; no particular isomorphism is named.
--
--   This is the affine computation identifying the two irreducible components of the special fibre $t = 0$ of a crossing chart $W[x,y]/(xy-t)$: each is an affine line over $W/(t)$, the two meeting where both coordinates vanish. It is used in the analysis of the charts of the resolution of $uv = t^e$, in particular in the description of the vanishing ideal of the closure of the lines and in the construction of a two-line affine cover of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_CrossingQuotient_exists_algEquiv_quotient_span_U_and_span_V_polynomial.lean

